au:AUM-4-8-001 a ac:Finding ;
    rdfs:label "Council of State report before creation" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom au:ProseSnapshot ;
    ac:alternativeReading "A predecessor could explain it, but none is established in the inspected passages; do not silently invent one." ;
    ac:audit au:Audit ;
    ac:claimGap "The exact commitments producing this consistency issue are not fully represented in the selected power-review graph. Source-passage evidence remains primary." ;
    ac:claimLinkNote "C01 supplies proposed discovery context and C06 the 1852 administration context. Neither extracts the exact receiving-body/creation pair." ;
    ac:classification cv:IntegrationMismatch ;
    ac:detectionBasis cv:ProseFirst ;
    ac:lifecycle cv:Open ;
    ac:normalizedScope "Same Californian body, spring 1848 report versus 1852 creation. The early report is in the locally PROPOSED CR-028 sequence; the reorganization has separate approval support." ;
    ac:passage au:F001-left,
        au:F001-right ;
    ac:reasoning "The named recipient appears before its stated creation; repeated character records do not establish a predecessor." ;
    ac:relatedClaim fg:C01,
        fg:C06 ;
    ac:repairOption "Retain 1852 and choose an existing recipient, or explicitly establish and distinguish an intended predecessor; author choice required." .

au:AUM-4-8-002 a ac:Finding ;
    rdfs:label "Gold secrecy count" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom au:ProseSnapshot ;
    ac:alternativeReading "A narrower political circle could contain five, but the phrase in the world does not state that scope. Seven is a lower bound, not a newly established exhaustive total." ;
    ac:audit au:Audit ;
    ac:claimGap "The exact commitments producing this consistency issue are not fully represented in the selected power-review graph. Source-passage evidence remains primary." ;
    ac:claimLinkNote "C01 represents proposed discovery and secrecy, but contains no count or enumerated knowledge set." ;
    ac:classification cv:Contradiction ;
    ac:detectionBasis cv:ProseFirst ;
    ac:lifecycle cv:Open ;
    ac:normalizedScope "The October 1847 Mokelumne find by the December 1847 bargain; both passages locally PROPOSED. The full line-125 context explicitly names four discoverers before three informed leaders." ;
    ac:passage au:F002-left,
        au:F002-right ;
    ac:reasoning "Four distinct discoverers plus three informed leaders imply at least seven knowers, inconsistent with the stated global total of five." ;
    ac:relatedClaim fg:C01 ;
    ac:repairOption "Use a non-exhaustive formulation or ask the author to reconcile count and disclosure sequence; do not silently replace five with an exhaustive seven." .

au:AUM-4-8-003 a ac:Finding ;
    rdfs:label "Unverifiable testimony becomes unqualified narration" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom au:ProseSnapshot ;
    ac:alternativeReading "Implicit focalization through Abigail could reconcile it, but the synopsis supplies no such attribution and approval preserves uncertainty." ;
    ac:audit au:Audit ;
    ac:claimGap "The exact commitments producing this consistency issue are not fully represented in the selected power-review graph. Source-passage evidence remains primary." ;
    ac:classification cv:IntegrationMismatch ;
    ac:detectionBasis cv:ProseFirst ;
    ac:lifecycle cv:Open ;
    ac:normalizedScope "Same pastor, Abigail and reported 1850 instruction. CR-022 retains unverifiable testimony; this is narrative stance, not uncertain settled kinship." ;
    ac:passage au:F003-left,
        au:F003-right ;
    ac:reasoning "Section 6 omits the attribution protecting the story in section 1. This is an integration/stance mismatch, not proof that the instruction was false." ;
    ac:repairOption "Attribute the instruction to Abigail’s account while preserving uncertainty; do not decide what was actually said." .

au:AUM-4-8-004 a ac:Finding ;
    rdfs:label "Edo treaty party after common foreign relations" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom au:ProseSnapshot ;
    ac:alternativeReading "Geographical shorthand or envoys acting with a common mandate could explain it. The inspected prose does not establish invalidity or sole treaty power." ;
    ac:audit au:Audit ;
    ac:claimGap "The exact commitments producing this consistency issue are not fully represented in the selected power-review graph. Source-passage evidence remains primary." ;
    ac:classification cv:MissingBridge ;
    ac:detectionBasis cv:ProseFirst ;
    ac:lifecycle cv:Open ;
    ac:normalizedScope "1858 treaty after the 1856 Confederation enters force; California as member state versus common external relations. Earlier pre-confederation contacts are separate." ;
    ac:passage au:F004-left,
        au:F004-right ;
    ac:reasoning "The text does not specify the capacity in which California concludes the treaty after external relations become common." ;
    ac:repairOption "Clarify the treaty party and envoys’ capacity consistently with the intended constitutional arrangement." .

au:AUM-4-8-005 a ac:Finding ;
    rdfs:label "Assay office before public confirmation versus 1850 opening" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom au:ProseSnapshot ;
    ac:alternativeReading "An earlier temporary or differently located office is plausible but unstated. Private assays at Carquinez do not establish a public office." ;
    ac:audit au:Audit ;
    ac:claimGap "The exact commitments producing this consistency issue are not fully represented in the selected power-review graph. Source-passage evidence remains primary." ;
    ac:claimLinkNote "C01 covers delayed public confirmation; C03 covers state receipts and mint context. Neither fully extracts assay-office identity and opening conditions." ;
    ac:classification cv:SuspectedContradiction ;
    ac:detectionBasis cv:ProseFirst ;
    ac:lifecycle cv:Open ;
    ac:normalizedScope "Public assay machinery required before October 1848 confirmation versus the San Francisco mint/office opening in 1850. Local proposed discovery timetable remains proposed." ;
    ac:passage au:F005-left,
        au:F005-right ;
    ac:reasoning "The sequence conflicts if these are the same public institution; the text does not establish that identity." ;
    ac:relatedClaim fg:C01,
        fg:C03 ;
    ac:repairOption "Distinguish an intended earlier office or align the opening condition; no earlier institution is invented here." .

